🏠 In the UAE, it is now possible to invest in real estate from the age of 18

Previously, individuals had to be at least 21 years old to purchase real estate independently. The minimum age requirement has now been lowered, creating new opportunities for young investors.

This is an important change for those who want to start building their investment portfolio at an earlier age, generate rental income, and benefit from Dubai’s growing real estate market.

In addition, this new regulation may be of interest to parents who are planning to invest in their children’s future and help them become property owners at a younger age.

Real estate in Dubai remains one of the most attractive investment opportunities, driven by strong rental demand, steady market growth, and investor-friendly conditions.

